WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:01.950
Hey, David.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:08.830
At what point would a military coup to remove
Trump not be the absolute worst option?

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.820
I'm really only half joking.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:15.309
So I think we have to be very careful about
these questions.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:20.090
Donald, I get why people are sort of worried
and tense about this.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.150
Donald Trump has floated the idea of delaying
the election.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.550
He's talked about it's going to be rigged.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:28.500
He almost certainly will claim some aspect
of it is rigged.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.730
He still hasn't even accepted the popular
vote results of 2016, which is an election

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.790
he won.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:39.350
You can be sure that he is going to find something
to take issue with in November.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.960
And certainly if he loses, he absolutely is
going to.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.550
I don't think it's going to come to anything
like a military coup.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.710
I, I.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.910
Most people in the audience seem to be on
board with me.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:57.989
And on the same page that January 20th, Trump,
if he loses or there is no election, he is

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:00.130
no longer the president.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:07.760
And it's on the one hand, not going to require
a military coup to remove Donald Trump.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.979
But on the other hand, I think that he's going
to go.

00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:17.250
I think he he you know, Sam Ceder earlier
this week talked about lawsuits and lawsuits

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.650
maybe going all the way up to the Supreme
Court.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.490
I don't think that that's totally implausible.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.969
And that's certainly a reason for us to try
to run up the score and have a huge popular

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:26.969
vote victory.

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:29.430
First step is not to lose in the popular vote.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:33.850
Next step is to have a big popular vote, big
victory, which hopefully will translate into

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.289
an Electoral College victory.

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:40.590
But we know the tricks that they're planning.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.359
There's foreign meddling going on again.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:46.959
Postmaster is trying to kneecap and cripple
the post office.

00:01:46.959 --> 00:01:49.209
They're trying to prevent mail in voting.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:52.579
And they're suing states in order to try to
do it.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.249
They're deregistering voters.

00:01:54.249 --> 00:01:56.450
They're trying to close polling place.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.750
We know all the tactics.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.319
The experts have looked at it.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.520
And here's the bottom line.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.329
All of these things can certainly have an
effect on the results.

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:09.459
If everybody goes out and votes, we overwhelm
it.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:13.510
All of these techniques only work when half
the country doesn't vote.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:19.250
If we actually get the vote out, these questions
of the military removing Trump or whatever,

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.019
they instantly become moot.

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:22.019
They really do.

00:02:22.019 --> 00:02:27.819
So I think that would I would encourage the
audience to do.

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:32.700
Is trust that the best remedy?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.400
Is for all of us to vote.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.650
All of these probably will Trump leave or
not?

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.180
Will we need the military to remove him?

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:46.560
An overwhelming defeat of Donald Trump in
both the popular and electoral votes is going

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.530
to prevent all of these issues if it's overwhelming.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:54.760
Even this Supreme Court with two of Donald
Trump's selections, Neil Gorsuch and Brett

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.840
Kavanaugh, is not going to do anything that
that would somehow allow Trump to stay in

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:00.840
power.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.639
The best remedy is every single person voting.

